lingmo-statusbar (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Phase 2, first step: the global menu. The bar now shows the menu titles of
    the active window, read from the window's com.canonical.dbusmenu object. The
    window advertises that object in the _KDE_NET_WM_APPMENU_SERVICE_NAME and
    _KDE_NET_WM_APPMENU_OBJECT_PATH X11 properties, which AppMenuTracker reads
    with libxcb; DbusMenuClient renders the layout and sends Event clicks back.
  * Menu titles open a fly-out submenu; deeper levels drill into the second
    column.
  * New headless regression test for the dbusmenu client
    (test/dbusmenu/run.sh, no display or DTK needed).
  * Build-Depends: libxcb1-dev.

 -- Lingmo OS Team <team@lingmo.org>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:55:00 +0800

lingmo-statusbar (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Phase 1 skeleton: full-width top bar window, application name of the active
    window pushed by a bundled KWin script, clock with a calendar popup,
    placeholder tray icons and a system menu that only logs its actions.

 -- Lingmo OS Team <team@lingmo.org>  Sat, 14 Feb 2026 10:00:00 +0800
